    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d359">

                <pb facs="0399" n="325" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg325"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/7690</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)<anchor n="2" xml:id="d359-f1"
                    />
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Circular telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-28T14:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 28, 1917, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In order to secure best results in cooperating with the Allies, the Department
                    feels that the American diplomatic missions should endeavor to establish with
                    Allied representatives as close and confidential relations as possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d359-f1" n="2" type="source" xml:id="d359-f1-content">
                <p>The same telegram (unnumbered), on the same date, to the Ambassadors in Great
                    Britain, Italy, Russia, Spain, and the Ministers in Switzerland, the
                    Netherlands, Sweden, Norway, and Denmark.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
